{{ if lookPath "nu" -}}
# A plain after hook runs after every apply. Its target name sorts after all
# install/reconcile/setup hooks, making this the actual completion summary.
#
# Guarded on `nu`: chezmoi hands this to [interpreters.nu] (`nu --stdin`) whenever
# it renders non-empty. On a fresh Windows box the after phase runs before mise's
# shims reach the process PATH — windows-system.ps1 persists them with
# SetEnvironmentVariable(..., "User"), which cannot mutate the running chezmoi
# process — so `nu` is unresolvable and the apply dies here. Rendering empty makes
# chezmoi skip the script instead.
if (which fastfetch | is-not-empty) {
    fastfetch
}
{{ end -}}
